Feature: Update volume paths in pyspark_script.py using volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx

  The pyspark_script.py must be updated so that only the volume paths for three CSV files
  (biomarker_readings.csv, patient_demographics.csv, site_details.csv) are replaced with their
  corresponding new paths as specified in volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx. All other logic and code
  must remain unchanged.

  Background:
    Given the original pyspark_script.py contains the following volume paths:
      | variable      | old_volume_path                                                                 |
      | biomarker_df  | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/biomarker_readings.csv      |
      | patient_df    | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/patient_demographics.csv    |
      | site_df       | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/site_details.csv           |
    And the volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx contains the following mappings:
      | old_volume_path                                                                 | new_volume_path                                                                                   |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/biomarker_readings.csv      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Biomarker.csv      |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/patient_demographics.csv    | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Patient_Demographics.csv |
      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/site_details.csv           | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Site_Data.csv      |

  Scenario: Happy path - Update all volume paths as per mapping sheet
    Given pyspark_script.py contains the old volume paths for biomarker_df, patient_df, and site_df
    When the script is updated using the mapping from volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx
    Then the volume paths in the following lines must be replaced:
      | variable      | new_volume_path                                                                                   |
      | biomarker_df  | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Biomarker.csv      |
      | patient_df    | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Patient_Demographics.csv |
      | site_df       | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Site_Data.csv      |
    And all other code, logic, and variable names remain unchanged

  Scenario Outline: Data-driven test - Update volume path for each file
    Given pyspark_script.py contains the old volume path "<old_volume_path>" for variable <variable>
    When the script is updated using the mapping from volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx
    Then the volume path for <variable> must be replaced with "<new_volume_path>"
    And no other changes are made to the script

    Examples:
      | variable      | old_volume_path                                                                 | new_volume_path                                                                                   |
      | biomarker_df  | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/biomarker_readings.csv      | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Biomarker.csv      |
      | patient_df    | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/patient_demographics.csv    | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Patient_Demographics.csv |
      | site_df       | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/site_details.csv           | /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/19_03_2025_Site_Data.csv      |

  Scenario: Error - Old volume path not found in mapping sheet
    Given pyspark_script.py contains a volume path "/Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/unknown_file.csv"
    When the script is updated using the mapping from volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx
    Then the volume path for unknown_file.csv must remain unchanged
    And an error message "No mapping found for volume path: /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/unknown_file.csv" must be logged

  Scenario: Error - Mapping sheet is missing required mapping
    Given volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx is missing the mapping for "/Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/site_details.csv"
    When the script is updated
    Then the volume path for site_df must remain unchanged
    And an error message "No mapping found for volume path: /Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/AD-218/site_details.csv" must be logged

  Scenario: Validation - Only volume path is changed, logic remains unchanged
    Given the original pyspark_script.py contains logic for data cleaning, aggregation, and joins
    When the volume paths are updated as per mapping sheet
    Then the following must be true:
      | validation_rule                                                                                 |
      | Only the file path string in spark.read.option("header", True).csv(...) is changed              |
      | All variable names, function calls, and processing logic remain identical                       |
      | No additional code, comments, or formatting changes are introduced                              |

  Scenario: Validation - Volume path format
    Given the new volume path is applied in pyspark_script.py
    Then the new volume path must match the format "/Volumes/agilisium_playground/purgo_playground/de_dq/clinical_trail/<file_name>.csv"
    And <file_name> must be one of:
      | file_name                        |
      | 19_03_2025_Biomarker.csv         |
      | 19_03_2025_Patient_Demographics.csv |
      | 19_03_2025_Site_Data.csv         |

  Scenario: Error - Invalid new volume path format
    Given the new volume path does not match the required format
    When the script is updated
    Then an error message "Invalid new volume path format for: <new_volume_path>" must be logged

  Scenario: Validation - No duplicate volume paths
    Given the mapping sheet is applied
    Then each old volume path must map to a unique new volume path
    And no two variables use the same new volume path

  Scenario: Validation - Script output after update
    Given the script is updated with new volume paths
    When the script is executed
    Then the output must be identical to the original script except for the updated file paths

  Scenario: Validation - Acceptance criteria
    Given the requirements
    Then the following acceptance criteria must be met:
      | criteria                                                                                       |
      | Only the volume paths for the three specified CSV files are updated                            |
      | All other code, logic, and variable names remain unchanged                                     |
      | The new volume paths are exactly as specified in volume_mapping_sheet.xlsx                     |
      | Any unmapped or invalid paths are logged as errors                                             |
      | The script remains syntactically and functionally correct                                      |
